<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">951–995</span> · Also known as Henry the Quarrelsome, Henry the Wrangler</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry the Quarrelsome was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 955 to 976 and again from 985 to 995, a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottonian-dynasty">Ottonian dynasty</a> and cousin of Emperor Otto II. His repeated rebellions led Otto to depose him and to split off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> as a separate duchy in 976, and after Otto's death in 983 he tried to seize the throne from the infant Otto III. His son became Emperor Henry II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Henry II, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_II_of_Bavaria2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
